 "answer": {
  "answer": "The goal was met. Five settings on five different scenes made the policy collide on every repeat: S8, S23, S37, S4 and S6. All five combine the same three changes: the key car comes later (+0.5 to +1 s), it is slowed (0.5x to 0.75x), and the ego is faster at hand-off (1.2x to 1.4x, with 1.4x in four of the five). Only S8 has enough repeats to put its failure rate clearly above 0.5. The other four have only three repeats each, so their lower bounds are only just above 0.5. Only three of the five are clear policy faults: S6, S37 and S4, where the policy steered left into a car in the next lane (S37 also braked hard for no reason). In S8 and S23 the gap to the lead car had already closed during the warm-up, and the hit came half a second after hand-off. Those two crashes were mostly set up before the policy took over, and the triage marks fault as unclear. No failure was flagged as a possible simulator artifact.",
