    "claim": "Confirmed failing case on 09a95ffa (car delayed 0.5 s at 0.75x, ego at 1.4x) and 0e899dd3 (car delayed 1 s at 0.75x, ego at 1.4x). In every repeat the ego hit the slower lead car's rear half a second after hand-off. By then the gap had already shrunk during the warm-up, and the policy braked only moderately. Fault is unclear: these crashes are mostly inherited from the replayed approach, so they show more about how the faster ego start sets up a collision than about the policy.",
